================================================================================================================

================================================================================================================
PART 0 -- runs: control, true LambdaCDM, the running window, and constant c_s^2 for contrast
================================================================================================================
  [PASS] SETUP-0  the hand-built (rho_b d_b + rho_cdm d_cdm)/(rho_b+rho_cdm) reproduces CLASS's own d_m transfer to < 1e-5 for every k >= 0.01 h/Mpc at every z, and the residual below that is the expected large-scale GAUGE term (CLASS's d_m is the gauge-invariant comoving density, d_b/d_cdm are synchronous): it falls by > 10x per decade from k = 1e-3 to 1e-1 h/Mpc at every z.  So the density weights are the code's own; the total spectrum below uses CLASS's d_m as its denominator, and sigma_8/P(k) at k >= 0.01 carry no error from this   (max |d_m(mine)/d_m(CLASS) - 1| (k >= 0.01) = 1.4e-06; residual at k = 1e-3/1e-2/1e-1 (z=0): 8.3e-06/1.0e-07/2.2e-09; (z=3): 7.2e-05/1.0e-06/2.8e-08)
  [PASS] SETUP-1  the TOTAL-matter sigma_8 of the c_s^2 = 0 fluid control equals that of a true LambdaCDM run (real CDM, no fluid) to < 0.5%, and my sigma_8 integral reproduces CLASS's own sigma8() for LambdaCDM to < 0.5%: the total-P(k) construction is validated at both ends   (sigma_8: control(total) 0.8226, LambdaCDM(total, mine) 0.8229, LambdaCDM (CLASS) 0.8228; CLASS's sigma8() of the control counts b+cdm only: 0.8193)
  [PASS] SETUP-2  and the control's total P(k, z=0) matches true LambdaCDM to < 1% for 0.01 < k < 10 h/Mpc   (max |P_ctrl/P_LCDM - 1| = 1.1e-03)
    runs done [1.2s]

