  [PASS] PK-0  THE INTENDED FEATURE IS THERE: at z = 0 the running fluid suppresses galaxy-scale total-matter power by half at k_50 = 0.4-0.8 h/Mpc across the window (P/P_ctrl < 0.35 at k = 1 h/Mpc, < 0.05 at 10 h/Mpc), while the large scales survive: < 1.5% at k = 0.1 h/Mpc for c0 = 1e-6   (k_50 = 0.79/0.59/0.44 h/Mpc; c0=1e-6: P/P at k=0.1: 0.9895, k=1: 0.320, k=10: 0.0134)
  [PASS] PK-1  sigma_8 (total matter) moves DOWN by 2-8% across the window -- a shift current S8 measurements (weak lensing sits 3-8% below Planck) cannot exclude and might even welcome; it is NOT a kill and NOT a win, and the check only asserts the size: |dsigma_8/sigma_8| < 10% for every window value   (sigma_8 = 0.8025 (-2.4%), 0.7880 (-4.2%), 0.7645 (-7.1%) vs control 0.8226)
  [PASS] PK-2  the BOSS/DESI regime is touched at the few-percent level: at z = 0.5 the total P(k) is suppressed by < 2% at k = 0.1 h/Mpc and < 10% at k = 0.3 h/Mpc for c0 = 1e-6 (a shape distortion that full-shape analyses can probe but which this lane does not adjudicate)   (z=0.5, c0=1e-6: P/P at k=0.1: 0.9971, 0.2: 0.9884, 0.3: 0.9740)
  [PASS] PK-3  CONTRAST -- the constant-c_s^2 (quadratic K) branch at the SAME c_s^2(today) = 1e-6 is dead on late-time structure alone: sigma_8 down by > 15% and P/P_ctrl < 0.05 at k = 1 h/Mpc (k_50 ~ 0.25 h/Mpc), confirming with a Boltzmann code what L129's growth solver found for p = 0   (const 1e-6: sigma_8 0.6711 (-18.4%), P/P(k=1) = 0.0037, k_50 = 0.25)

